Subject: [PATCH 527/527] [DS4.1] CED replay test: a decoder stack on the
 TileLang kernels under several chunkings

Three sliding-window decoder layers run each prefill step through the model
state's CED staging, the decoder's token metadata, the window metadata and
the sparse MLA. A layer writes its input as the step's kept rows' KV
records into a cache that starts as NaN, and the next layer's input is its
input plus its heads' output, so a row depends on every row it saw on the
way up and an unwritten read shows as NaN.

A 1,024-row prompt start plus a final chunk of 1, 64, 128 or 129 rows, as
one chunk, in 512- and 384-row chunks and after a prefix hit at 448: the
rows from the floor on are the single chunk's, bit for bit, and finite.
